; SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
; uses: core, names
;
; The lock file beside an IDL file, such as interfaces/aspis/catalog/
; v1.idl.lock (ADR 0067, rule 7; docs/design/call-language.md, "The lock
; and the canonical form"). Each entry is a published minor of the file's
; major, and the SHA3-256 hash of that minor's canonical form, in
; lowercase hex. The entries are the minors 0, 1, 2 and on, in order, one
; each, and the file's major is the IDL file's: idlc checks both, which
; this grammar doesn't say. A lock with no entries means nothing is
; published yet.

idl-lock      = *lock-comment *lock-entry
lock-comment  = "#" *lock-char %x0A            ; the SPDX tags, and a title
lock-char     = %x09 / %x20-7E / utf8-2 / utf8-3 / utf8-4
lock-entry    = major "." minor SP %s"sha3-256" SP 64hex %x0A
